        "text": "# try…catch\n\n`try...catch` is used to test a block of code for errors while it runs. If something goes wrong, it allows the program to jump to a backup plan instead of crashing the webpage completely.\n\nThink of your code like a trapeze artist performing a high-wire act. Most of the time, the performance goes perfectly. But in the event that something goes wrong, you want a safety net to catch you.\n\n",
